{%- doc -%}
  SixthGear Studios: hides the review sections ("What our customers say" carousel and the product
  review widget) until the store has at least the number of real reviews set in Theme settings >
  SixthGear: reviews (default 5). The count is Judge.me's own store-wide total
  (shop.metafields.judgeme.all_reviews_count). On a product page, the product review widget's
  section is also hidden while that product has no reviews of its own. Rendered in the head, so
  nothing flashes on screen.

  @example
  {% render 'sgs-reviews-gate' %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign jm = shop.metafields.judgeme
  assign count = jm.all_reviews_count.value | default: jm.all_reviews_count | plus: 0
  assign min = settings.sgs_reviews_min | default: 5 | plus: 0
  assign keys = settings.sgs_reviews_sections | default: 'sgs_reviews_carousel' | remove: ' ' | split: ','
-%}
{%- if count < min -%}
  <style>
    {% for key in keys %}{% if key != blank %}.shopify-section[id$='__{{ key | escape }}']{% unless forloop.last %}, {% endunless %}{% endif %}{% endfor %} {
      display: none !important;
    }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The product review widget on a product with no reviews of its own: Judge.me shows nothing there,
  so its section is hidden too, leaving no empty band
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign widget_key = settings.sgs_reviews_widget_section | strip -%}
{%- if template.name == 'product' and product != blank and widget_key != blank -%}
  {%- capture product_count -%}{% render 'sgs-product-review-count', product_resource: product %}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign product_count = product_count | strip | plus: 0 -%}
  {%- if product_count == 0 -%}
    <style>
      .shopify-section[id$='__{{ widget_key | escape }}'] {
        display: none !important;
      }
    </style>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
